1:Heroes
2:[$0000FF]Gather resources:
3:Malcolm:|Builder. The first storehouse plan you place will be free. Ability to recruit a Laborers Captain. Thanks to his knowledge, he quickly destroys buildings.
4:Eryt:|Builder. Malcolm's assistant. The bow isn't his strong suit, but it always comes in handy.
5:New Hero:
6:Prince Tyrio:|Prince of Hanrain. Doubles fish production. Ability to build ships. Accurately attacks the enemy with his arrows.
7:General Tamaio:|Main general of Hanrain's army. Prince Tyrio's assistant. A four-meter shield bearer with incredible durability and strength.
8:King Viren:|Lord of Andaro. An experienced warrior. His "Maw" formation has won many an attack.
9:Urno:|Spy. No one knows why he does what he doe. With the information he possesses, he can outwit anyone, even the king. 
10:Ethyria:|Princess of Cronwell. With her daggers, she'll quickly dispatch enemies at close quarters.
11:[$0000FF]Recruit an army:
12:King Dyron:|Lord of Hanrain. He possesses armor constructed on earth by General X, resembling the original armor found on Kamstar.
13:King Drein:|Lord of Nir Stronghold. Can train berserkers.
14:Princess Attilia:|A skilled crossbowwoman, daughter of King Karion. Thanks to her accuracy, she can kill any opponent. Speeds up the training of citizens.
15:King Alan:|His specialty is the two-handed long sword. Thanks to the techniques taught to him by his father, he is adept at dispatching enemies. Can train Wreckers. Devastators gain increased defense.
16:Dyron:|Thanks to the Glove of Destruction, he can easily demolish buildings and defeat enemies. The longer the effect is charged, the more powerful the energy blast will be.